## About this title\n\n### Synopsis\n\nOut now with a preface by Franco Bertoni, an essay by Francesco Alberoni and a postscript by Germano Celant, The Non-materiality of the Material is a monograph that presents not only the projects over a period of 20 years but also aphorisms and writings of Claudio Silvestrin. “I have learned from, and been inspired by, the great Italian masters: with superb style they teach us about the spiritual quality of materials, and the emotion of solidity that a form or configuration must embody and express in order to transcend the ordinary and the temporary. I've learned to go beyond material boundaries in order to render the potential infinity of things. Creating forms that make us feel the lack of durability and inevitable dissolution of the matter that we ourselves are made of.”\n\n\"About this title\" may belong to another edition of this title.\n\n### Seller's business information\n\nLIBRO CO. ITALIA S.R.L.\nVia Etruria 2/4/6, San Casciano in Val di Pesa, FI, 50026, Italy\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nClaudio Silvestrin: Books - AbeBooks (https://www.abebooks.com/book-search/title/claudio-silvestrin/book/)\nciteturn35search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 months ago; ISBN 10: 8842220167 / ISBN 13: 9788842220169 ... ISBN 10: 8842220167 / ISBN 13: 9788842220169\n## Claudio Silvestrin\n\nFranco Bertoni\n\nLanguage: English\n\nPublished by Birkhauser, 1999\n\nISBN 10: 0817661050 / ISBN 13: 9780817661052\n\nSeller: Moe's Books, Berkeley, CA, U.S.A.\n\n(4-star seller) Seller rating 4 out of 5 stars Image: 4-star rating, Learn more about seller ratings\n\nContact seller\n\nFirst Edition\n\nUsed - Hardcover\nCondition: Fine\n\nUS$ 50.00\n\nUS$ 6.50 shipping Learn more about shipping rates\nShips within U.S.A.\n\nQuantity: 1 available\n\nAdd to basket\n\nHardcover. Condition: Fine. Dust Jacket Condition: Fine. First Edition. Translated by Lucinda Byatt.\n\n  * Stock Image\n\n## Claudio Sil